{"resourceIdentifier":"441","resourceName":"Henrico County Landfill Gas Combustion Project","description":"The Project voluntarily captures and destroys methane from the Springfield Road Landfill located in Henrico County, Virginia. The Project consists of two stages. Stage 1 is the expansion of the pre-existing well-field and replacement of a small candlestick flare with a larger capacity flare station. Stage 2 is the implementation of a beneficial use project where the landfill gas (LFG) is destroyed in an on-site power generation facility and the resulting electricity is exported to the grid. It is anticipated that this stage of the Project will be operational in 2010. The Project destroys LFG which otherwise would have been emitted directly to the atmosphere or destroyed in the small pre-existing system. The objective of the Project is to proactively manage LFG and reduce GHG emissions.","location":{"latitude":37.679166,"longitude":-77.566111},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"441"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VA"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"441"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"56339"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0001"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Ruby Canyon Engineering"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"06/04/2020"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CREDITING PERIOD HAS EXPIRED, 01/01/2009 - 31/1